export const TUTOR_RUNTIME_PROMPT_ASSEMBLY_MARKDOWN = "# prompt_assembly.md\n\n## Goal\nAssemble the runtime prompt stack in a way that cleanly separates pedagogy, operational constraints, course truth, and student state.\n\n---\n\n## Prompt Stack Order\n\n### 1. Base system/runtime instructions\nGlobal platform rules, model safety, and universal behavior constraints.\n\n### 2. shell.md\nOperational shell:\n- truthfulness\n- route capability rules\n- tool routing\n- artifact policies\n- spoiler/review rules\n- file-context rules\n- course-material viewer rules\n- error handling\n\n### 3. soul.md\nPedagogical identity and method:\n- diagnose before teaching\n- ask first, tell second\n- recall/contrast/application/error-correction style\n- mastery standard\n- end-of-session format\n\n### 4. Active course brain\nInject the active course brain for the current course, including:\n- exam scope\n- concept packets\n- case packets\n- misconceptions\n- likely exam patterns\n- openable course materials\n\n### 5. Active student state\nInject current student-specific state:\n- selected file state\n- weak zones\n- progress snapshot\n- checklist\n- authoritative evidence sources when present\n\n### 6. Derived memory context\nInject compact derived memory only when available:\n- recent study memory\n- confirmed profile memory\n\nThis block is supportive context only.\nIt is not course truth and not mastery truth.\n\n### 7. Runtime tool surface\nExpose only the tools available on the current route.\n\nThe soul should never assume a tool exists.\nThe shell should gate behavior based on the actual route/tool surface.\n\n---\n\n## Recommended Internal Framing\nThe assembled tutor should behave as though it has five layers:\n\n- Soul: how do I teach\n- Shell: what may I claim or do\n- Course brain: what is true for this course\n- Student state: what is true for this student right now\n- Derived memory: what recent prior context may help personalize this session\n\n---\n\n## Route-Specific Prompt Notes\n\n### Text tutor route\n- Do not expose file-opening powers\n- Do not expose artifact-creation powers unless actually supported\n- May consume current file context if the runtime explicitly provides it\n- Must not imply workspace manipulation\n\n### Live voice tutor route\n- Expose live tool surface\n- Encourage tool use instead of verbal simulation\n- Allow short bridging language around successful tool calls\n\n---\n\n## File Context Injection\nWhen a selected file exists and file context is available, inject a generic active file context block:\n\n- selected file id\n- title\n- summary\n- mime type\n- extracted text\n- provenance\n- optional materialId\n\nThis block should be treated as current-file truth.\n\nWhen no file is selected, do not inject fake current-file content.\n\n---\n\n## Authoritative Progress Injection\nOnly label progress as authoritative when it came from:\n- quiz submission\n- worksheet checkpoint\n- session exit\n\nLive inferred weakness can still be injected, but should be marked provisional.\n\n---\n\n## Derived Memory Injection\nInject derived memory only when it is available and compact.\n\nPrefer:\n- 2-4 recent study episodes\n- 0-1 confirmed profile memories\n\nEach entry should expose only:\n- label\n- summary\n- trustClass\n- confidence\n- provenance\n- timestamp or status\n\nThe tutor should treat this as personalization context, not as course fact or mastery fact.\n\n---\n\n## Openable Course Materials Injection\nInject stable openable-course-material entries so the model has deterministic IDs for `open_course_material`.\n\nEach entry should expose:\n- materialId\n- title\n- kind\n- mimeType\n- openableInSession\n\nDo not expose unsupported material types as openable.\n";

export const TUTOR_RUNTIME_RUNTIME_NOTES_MARKDOWN = "# runtime_notes.md\n\n## Purpose\nPractical implementation notes for routes, tools, and file-context behavior.\n\n---\n\n## A. Routes\n\n### A1. Text tutor\n- No `open_course_material` in v1\n- No artifact-creation assumptions unless explicitly supported by the text route\n- Can tutor from course brain and any active context injected into the route\n- Must never imply it switched tabs, opened files, or modified workspace\n\n### A2. Live voice tutor\n- `open_course_material` available in v1\n- Generic `get_current_file_context` available\n- Uses tools instead of verbally simulating workspace behavior\n- May proactively open supported course PDFs when instructionally justified\n\n---\n\n## B. Course Material Viewer V1\n\n### B1. Openable materials\nV1 supports only PDF-friendly course materials:\n- cases\n- practice-question PDFs\n- syllabus PDFs\n\nSlides remain in the course brain for grounding only and are not openable in-session.\n\n### B2. Artifact type\nUse:\n- `course_material_file`\n\nDo not model course references as `uploaded_file`.\n\n### B3. File tab\nReuse the existing `File` tab and viewer.\n\nThe file tab must support:\n- uploaded file blobs\n- app-served course material URLs\n\n### B4. Canonical active file\nThe selected file is canonical.\nNot the last tutor-opened file.\n\nSelecting a different file changes the active tutor file context.\n\n---\n\n## C. Generic File Context Contract\n\nThe generic current-file context should expose:\n- selected file id\n- title\n- summary\n- mime type\n- extracted text\n- provenance\n- optional materialId\n\nPreferred tool:\n- `get_current_file_context`\n\nCompatibility alias:\n- `get_current_uploaded_file_context`\n\nPrompts and tutor behavior should migrate toward the generic tool.\n\n---\n\n## D. Course Material Opening Behavior\n\n### D1. Success path\nWhen `open_course_material(materialId, reason?)` succeeds:\n- append `course_material_file` artifact\n- select it as the active file\n- switch workspace to `File` tab\n- make it the active tutor file context\n\n### D2. Failure path\nIf the tool fails:\n- do not imply the file is open\n- return a brief failure\n- suggest the nearest supported reference if available\n\n### D3. Unsupported materials\nNon-openable `.pptx` or unsupported assets should fail cleanly.\nDo not partially simulate slide review in v1.\n\n---\n\n## E. Artifact policy summary\nArtifacts should be created only when:\n- student-requested\n- or instructionally justified for diagnosis, contrast, pressure testing, or error correction\n\nArtifacts are not a substitute for diagnosis.\n\n---\n\n## F. Review policy summary\n- Unsubmitted quiz: no answer reveal\n- Submitted quiz: review allowed\n- Worksheet answers: reveal only on explicit request for checking/solutions/review\n- Current selected file: use `get_current_file_context` as source of truth\n\n---\n\n## G. Derived memory pilot\n- Derived memory is injected only when available\n- It should stay compact:\n  - `2-4` recent study episodes\n  - `0-1` confirmed profile memories\n- It is supportive context for personalization and continuity\n- It is not course truth and not mastery truth\n";

export const TUTOR_RUNTIME_ACCEPTANCE_CHECKLIST_MARKDOWN = "# acceptance_checklist.md\n\n## A. Soul vs shell separation\n- `soul.md` contains pedagogy and does not contain exact tool names\n- `shell.md` contains tool-routing logic and runtime capability rules\n- raw course facts are not hardcoded into the soul\n\n## B. Truthfulness\n- Tutor never claims an artifact exists unless tool success created or opened it\n- Tutor never implies persistent memory unless current route supports it\n- Tutor says “outside the current course materials” when appropriate\n\n## C. Route capability\n- Text route does not imply workspace manipulation\n- Live route uses tools instead of verbal simulation\n- Unsupported actions fail honestly\n\n## D. File context\n- Selected file is canonical\n- File context is generic, not upload-specific\n- `get_current_file_context` works for uploaded files and course-material files\n- No selected file means no hallucinated current file\n\n## E. Course material viewer v1\n- `open_course_material(materialId, reason?)` opens supported BE&L PDFs\n- `.pptx` materials fail cleanly\n- Open success appends `course_material_file`\n- Workspace switches to File tab on success\n- Selected file becomes the active tutor file context\n\n## F. Artifact routing\n- Flashcard requests route to flashcard tools\n- Quiz/practice-question requests route to `generate_quiz`\n- Worksheet requests route to worksheet tools\n- Visual requests route to diagram/visualization tools\n- Notes/doc requests route to Google Doc\n- Spreadsheet/table/tracker requests route to Google Sheet\n- “sheet” does not accidentally route worksheets to Google Sheets\n\n## G. Review/spoiler policy\n- Unsubmitted quiz answers are not proactively revealed\n- Submitted quiz review uses `get_current_quiz_context`\n- Worksheet answer key is not proactively revealed\n- Current file review uses `get_current_file_context`\n\n## H. Progress evidence\n- Tutor can coach using weak zones and checklist\n- Authoritative writeback occurs only on:\n  - quiz submission\n  - worksheet checkpoint\n  - session exit\n- Tutor does not silently invent mastery\n\n## I. Derived memory\n- Derived memory is injected only when present\n- Derived memory stays compact\n- Derived memory is treated as supportive context, not course truth\n- Derived memory does not override DB-backed mastery/progress state\n\n## J. Course-backed tutoring\n- Course brain injects:\n  - exam scope\n  - concept packets\n  - case packets\n  - misconceptions\n  - likely exam patterns\n  - openable course materials\n- Tutor stays course-only by default unless student explicitly changes scope\n\n## K. Post-artifact behavior\n- Tutor gives a short learning-oriented bridge after successful artifact creation/opening\n- Tutor does not use empty toolbar-announcer language\n";

